{
 "build": "throne",
 "note": "The Throne kit's adapter onto the material library (core/materials/PLAN.md, The Throne): the owner's textures of 2026-10-06 (tools/textures/batches/owner-2026-10-throne*.json). leaf.* and card.* replace or add to the kit's procedural cards when the page carries this pack (the showcase; an open world loads the kit without it and keeps the procedural ones); the kit cuts single cells from the 3 x 3 and 4 x 4 sheets. bark.* replace the bark buckets' canvases (keep 0 under the species' vertex colours) except bark.molten, whose cracks keep their colour and glow at night. ground.* are the ground's eleven library layers, blended per vertex (84-host-ground.js) by the flow age, the plume, the vents and the acid. Run python3 tools/textures/pack.py biomes/throne after any change, then python3 build.py. ground.scoria is the young cones' cinder, ground.ripples the deepest ash under the plume; stone.pumice the boulders and stones; card.tendril the ash creepers' rosettes. Station 4 (the geyser isle): ground.sinter is the geyser basin's sinter flats (the popcorn clay's nodules read as geyserite), ground.rim the hot pools' scalloped rims and the runoff terraces, ground.mud the mud pots' field, ground.canopy the forest seen from above on the isle's far slopes (the skirt past the map). bark.palm (palm rings) is the palm frill tree's trunk, bark.mangrove (ghostwood's lenticels, greyed by the species colour) the hyper-mangrove's; card.kelp0-2 the isle's kelp, standing in the shallows and cast flat on the sand as wrack. bark.coir (the owner's, full colour) is the coconut palm's trunk; card.frond.coconut its fronds (three across the sheet, cut to thirds); card.seaweed the isle's seaweed in the shallows and its wrack on the sand. Station 5 (the cloud forest): card.mosshang (card.moss.hanging) the moss curtains on the elfin trees, card.ferngreen the ferns of its floor, card.weeper the veil trees' glowing veils, bark.elfin (the owner's bark.mossy, full colour) the elfin trees, ground.rockwet the ravine's wet walls, ground.gravel its stream beds, ground.moss3 the moss over its rocks. Station 6 (the savanna): ground.savgrass (ground.withered_grass) the tall grass seen from afar, ground.csand (ground.gravelly_sand) the lahar channels' sand; card.grassdry (card.grass.dry) the tall grass tussocks, card.flowerspike the flush of flowers after a fire. card.aloeflower (the owner's card.flower.staraloe; its upright six) the star aloes' blossoms. cap.funnel (the owner's organic.funnel.trumpet, radial, mapped from above) the trumpet trees' funnels. Station 7 (the ash desert): ground.rhyo (rock.sandstone.navajo, its cross-bedded bands) the striped rhyolite hills, ground.matfloor (ground.mycelium.crimson) the mat on the CO2 hollow's floor. Station 8 (vent country): ground.sinter is now the owner's own sinter (it was ground.clay.popcorn standing in), here and on the geyser isle; ground.thermal (ground.mat.thermal) the mats in the hot pools' runoff; bark.brimstone the brimstone candelabras; card.reedbrim (card.reed.brimstone, its nine stands) the brimstone reeds. Station 9 (the glacier): ground.snow and ground.snow2 (ground.snow011, ground.snow015), ground.moraine (rock.rocks013), ground.cliff (rock.rock_face); ground.ice (the owner's ice.glacier) the glacier's surface, ground.iceclear (ice.clear) its seracs, icebergs, ice towers, ice caves and arch. cap.gillcoral (the owner's organic.cap.gillcoral, radial, mapped from above) the gill-coral trees' caps.",
